  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.Narayana vs State Of Andhra Pradesh on 1 October, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.6060 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "1. In this Criminal Petition filed under Section 482 of Cr.P.C., the petitioner/accused No.1 seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.180 of 2019 of New Port Police Station, Visakhapatnam City, which was registered against him for the offences under Sections 270, 272, 273, 328 and 511 of IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short, 'the FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that, on 26.09.2019 at 12:00 hours, on receiving the credible information, the complainant suo motu registered the case against the petitioner/Accused No.1 on the ground that he is in possession of the banned tobacco products, having purchased the same from one Pedababu of Bada Bazar, Berhampur of Odisha, transporting the same to various shops in Gajuwaka for sale on higher prices and on interrogation as the accused voluntarily confessed to have been engaged in the business of prohibited tobacco products, seized the same, registered F.I.R., and remanded him to judicial custody for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore UDPR,J registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
